5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71"></path></svg>Practical Example</h2></a><p clas=
s=3D"text-wrap font-ibm-plex font-light !text-base md:!text-[1.15rem] !text=
-stone-200 not-first:mt-[1.25em] leading-7">Container Blueprints (e.g., Cli=
ent App, API Server, Database) are typically established at the start of a =
project and evolve as infrastructure grows.</p><p class=3D"text-wrap font-i=
bm-plex font-light !text-base md:!text-[1.15rem] !text-stone-200 not-first:=
mt-[1.25em] leading-7"><strong><strong>Product Manager defines features:</s=
trong></strong> "Checkout" (auto-initializes: <code>Checkout</code> FRD \+ =
<code>Checkout</code> Feature Blueprint) "Order Tracking" (auto-initializes=
: <code>Order Tracking</code> FRD \+ <code>Order Tracking</code> Feature Bl=
ueprint)</p><p class=3D"text-wrap font-ibm-plex font-light !text-base md:!t=
ext-[1.15rem] !text-stone-200 not-first:mt-[1.25em] leading-7"><strong><str=
ong>Product Manager writes structured requirements into the FRDs:</strong><=
/strong> =E2=86=92 Checkout (REQ-CHECKOUT-001, REQ-CHECKOUT-002, =E2=80=A6)=
 =E2=86=92 Order Tracking (REQ-TRACK-001, REQ-TRACK-002, =E2=80=A6)</p><p c=
lass=3D"text-wrap font-ibm-plex font-light !text-base md:!text-[1.15rem] !t=
ext-stone-200 not-first:mt-[1.25em] leading-7"><strong><strong>Engineer rea=
ds requirements and identifies shared system capabilities, creates Componen=
t Blueprints:</strong></strong> =E2=86=92 Identity and Session Management (=
containing components like <code>AuthenticationService</code>, <code>Sessio=
nTokenStore</code>, <code>UserProfileClient</code>) =E2=86=92 Notification =
Delivery (containing components like <code>NotificationRouter</code>, <code=
>EmailDeliveryService</code>, <code>SmsDeliveryService</code>)</p><p class=
=3D"text-wrap font-ibm-plex font-light !text-base md:!text-[1.15rem] !text-=
stone-200 not-first:mt-[1.25em] leading-7"><strong><strong>Engineer writes =
Feature Blueprints:</strong></strong> =E2=86=92 Checkout Feature Blueprint =
(composes Identity and Session Management \+ checkout-specific components) =
=E2=86=92 Order Tracking Feature Blueprint (composes Identity and Session M=
anagement \+ Notification Delivery \+ order-tracking-specific components)</=
p><p class=3D"text-wrap font-ibm-plex font-light !text-base md:!text-[1.15r=
em] !text-stone-200 not-first:mt-[1.25em] leading-7">The engineer's job: (1=
) identify shared capabilities that underpin features, (2) document them as=
 Component Blueprints, (3) compose them into Feature Blueprints that map on=
to Requirements. Container and Component Blueprints form the system's <stro=
ng><strong>foundation</strong></strong> =E2=80=94 Container Blueprints esta=
blish the infrastructure context early and evolve as the platform grows; Co=
mponent Blueprints capture reusable capabilities within and across those co=
ntainers. Feature Blueprints are driven by product requirements and compose=
 what the foundation provides. The ideal outcome is that Feature Blueprints=
 are mostly <em>composition</em>; feature-specific components exist where n=
eeded. Components often start in Feature Blueprints and are refactored into=
 Component Blueprints when reuse emerges =E2=80=94 that lifecycle is expect=
ed.</p><a class=3D"group relative block tracking-none scroll-mt-[85px] -ml-=
