-first:mt-[1.25em] leading-7">Relationships between components are describe=
d in <strong><strong>natural language paragraphs</strong></strong> that act=
 as the <strong><strong>edges</strong></strong> of the architecture: what f=
lows between components, who depends on whom, and why.</p><p class=3D"text-=
wrap font-ibm-plex font-light !text-base md:!text-[1.15rem] !text-stone-200=
 not-first:mt-[1.25em] leading-7"><strong><strong>Key principles:</strong><=
/strong> Use each paragraph to connect concrete components defined via <cod=
e>component</code> blocks; mention both components early so the edge is exp=
licit. State direction (who depends on whom). Use component mentions (<code=
>#...</code>) and element mentions (<code>...</code>) to add implementation=
 detail and data-flow clarity, not as ends in themselves. Explain <em>why</=
em>, not just <em>what</em>. One relationship per paragraph, 2-4 sentences.=
 Do not restate component block responsibilities; describe the <em>interact=
ion</em> and what crosses the boundary.</p><a class=3D"group relative block=
