md:!text-[1.15rem] !text-stone-200 not-first:mt-[1.25em] leading-7">A Conta=
iner Blueprint is the technical specification for a C4 container: a separat=
ely deployable or runnable unit in the system. It documents the container's=
 technology choices, runtime environment, cross-cutting infrastructure, and=
 the boundaries it presents to components within it and to other containers=
. Container Blueprints are feature-agnostic and infrastructure-focused.</p>=
<p class=3D"text-wrap font-ibm-plex font-light !text-base md:!text-[1.15rem=
] !text-stone-200 not-first:mt-[1.25em] leading-7"><strong><strong>Create a=
 Container Blueprint when:</strong></strong> you're establishing or documen=
ting a deployable unit =E2=80=94 a web application, API server, task worker=
, data layer (schema management, migration strategy, access patterns), or C=
I/CD pipeline. Container Blueprints are especially valuable when the contai=
ner has cross-cutting concerns like authentication, middleware, error handl=
ing, or observability that affect all components hosted within it, or when =
multiple Component Blueprints reference the same container and would benefi=
t from a single source of truth about its characteristics.</p><a class=3D"g=
roup relative block tracking-none scroll-mt-[85px] -ml-8 pl-8 text-inherit"=
 id=3D"component-blueprint-guidance" href=3D"https://www.8090.ai/docs/opini=
ons/blueprint-writing-guide#component-blueprint-guidance"><h2 class=3D"rela=
