ding-7"><strong><strong>Title and feature summary</strong></strong> =E2=80=
=94 Start with the Blueprint title, then add <code>## Feature Summary</code=
> with a 2=E2=80=933 sentence user-centered summary that references the cor=
responding Requirements Document.  </li><li class=3D"list-item font-ibm-ple=
x-sans font-light !text-base md:!text-[1.15rem] !text-stone-200 not-first:m=
t-[1.25em] leading-7"><strong><strong>Component Blueprint composition</stro=
ng></strong> =E2=80=94 Add <code>## Component Blueprint Composition</code> =
to document which shared capabilities this feature composes and how each is=
 configured or scoped. Use document mentions (<code>@...</code>) for refere=
nced Blueprints/Requirements and component mentions (<code>#...</code>) for=
 concrete runtime components involved in the composition. Use composition p=
aragraphs to explain how each capability wires into the feature, stating di=
rection and data flow.  </li><li class=3D"list-item font-ibm-plex-sans font=
-light !text-base md:!text-[1.15rem] !text-stone-200 not-first:mt-[1.25em] =
